{"request_sha256": "3425c510ff1b19beecf23610e7d2b457d5b750224dcdeaac2d2af2f7840694b1", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "0f33fd2397d9a7c2fcbcbc0e34e3e9aced419207548001a3aff0a5becd95cfd6", "schema_sha256": "30f41622e6c7560e23f9cf8ab8aee356761b3ddea7cb1a9d1835cabc34f30ac0", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 7107}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "unknown", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["crown-pinnate-arching-fronds (core): in render-0 and render-1 the crown is a flat starburst of ~25-35 straight, radially spread axes of near-equal length with no arching and no downward recurve; no frond hangs below the crown insertion point. reference-0 shows long fronds curving outward then strongly downward, with the lowest fronds drooping well below the crown base and the crown outline reading as a rounded shuttlecock. Defining mismatch.", "owner-fronds-long-arching (owner priority 1): frond length in render-0/render-1 is roughly 0.15-0.2 of trunk height and the axes are nearly bare; in reference-0 frond length is a large fraction of trunk length and the blades are dense and heavy. The owner's named first dials (leaflet size, frond length) are not yet moved to reference scale at either seed.", "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow (core): leaflets in render-0/render-1/render-2 read as sparse dark speckles and short stubs scattered along thin rachides, with large gaps of bare axis; the frond has no plumose V-sectioned mass and no bristly continuous margin. reference-0/reference-1/reference-2 show densely inserted narrow stiff leaflets in groups at differing angles. Defining mismatch.", "owner-trunk-straight-constant (owner priority 2): the trunk in render-0 and render-2 is distinctly wavy - an S-curve in the upper third plus an angular knee/bulge at mid-height where the silhouette steps outward; render-1 (seed 42) is straighter overall but still carries a visible waviness and the same mid-trunk knee. reference-0 shows a smooth single lean/curve and reference-1/reference-2 are essentially straight; none is wavy. Defining mismatch at both seeds.", "solitary-columnar-stem (core): the single unbranched stem is supported, but the render trunk is not columnar of roughly constant diameter - it tapers markedly from a flared base to a narrow apex and carries a local bulge at the mid-trunk kink (render-0, render-2). reference-1/reference-2 show near-constant diameter over the visible span.", "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern (core): the render trunk surface is smooth and untextured over its whole visible length in render-0, render-1 and render-2 - no stubs, no spiral, no lattice. reference-1/reference-2 show a coarse spiral diamond lattice of projecting leaf-base stubs. Reported as drawn; the owner states fn-110 has not landed, which explains the state but does not resolve the trait.", "trunk-fibrous-matting (core): no fibre, husk or shaggy interstitial material anywhere on the render trunk (render-0, render-2), against the packed reddish-brown matting filling the lattice in reference-1/reference-2. Same scope caveat as the leaf-base pattern; still an unmet core trait.", "fruit-clusters-pendent (core): no inflorescence stalks or fruit bunches are drawn at the crown in render-0 or render-1; reference-0 shows two to three heavy pendent orange-red bunches emerging among the frond bases. The owner scopes fn-111 out of this pass, which is not evidence of resolution.", "P-BASE cell unassessable: render-3 is a near-full-frame flat black silhouette wedge against sky and ground with no resolvable surface, so leaf-base-close cannot be judged; the joint input also records render-3 visibility as hidden."], "observations": ["Both P-WHOLE seeds share the same crown construction: a single apical point emitting straight thin axes in a near-planar radial fan, with the longest axes roughly horizontal and none descending below the insertion.", "Seed variation between render-0 and render-1 is confined to trunk curvature magnitude and slight crown asymmetry; the frond length, leaflet density and trunk surface are identical in character, so the core failures are not seed-specific.", "render-2 (P-TRUNK) is the clearest view of the trunk surface: a smooth shaded tube with a soft specular gradient and no geometric or textured detail at any height.", "The trunk is bare of any epiphytes, sprouts or foliage in both P-WHOLE renders, matching the owner's third priority; note the reference epiphytic ferns in reference-1/reference-2 are scene features the inventory itself records as variation, not species character.", "Finish quality relative to anchor-0 (spruce): the render's ground plane, sky gradient and trunk shading are at a comparable stylistic level, but the foliage reads as aliased speckle rather than the anchor's coherent needle mass. The anchor bears on finish only and no morphology conclusion is drawn from it.", "frond-colour-range (variation, uncertain in the inventory): the render foliage is a dark desaturated green with black speckling in render-0/render-1 and a brighter green in render-2; this sits within the inventory's recorded reference colour spread and is treated as acceptable variation, not a defect.", "trunk-lean-and-curve is a recorded variation trait in the inventory (leaning/S-curved in reference-0 vs straight in reference-1/reference-2); the render's failure is not the lean but the high-frequency waviness and the angular mid-trunk knee, which no reference shows.", "dead-frond-skirt, petiole-base-orange-sheath, crown-shaft-absent, basal-leaflet-spines and trunk-colour-and-weathering are secondary refinements; their absence is recorded but not treated as blocking.", "Improvement over any prior state is not assessed here and would not substitute for the unmet core traits."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown is a flat radial starburst of short straight sparse axes at both seeds; no arching, no drooping lower fronds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with frond length and leaflet size dials still being far below reference scale and with little or no gravity/curvature applied to the rachis, as the owner's priority wording anticipates; the mechanism is not established by the images."}, {"observation": "Leaflets render as sparse speckles and short stubs along bare rachides rather than a dense plumose blade.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Could be leaflet size/count below threshold, or a rasterisation/alpha issue at this pixel scale; both are candidates and neither is established."}, {"observation": "Trunk is wavy with an S-curve and an angular mid-height knee, and tapers with a local bulge rather than holding near-constant diameter.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The host note records the palm's taper value at 1.0, outside the authored 0.05-0.6 range, and identifies the trunk as where the owner wants that dial; this is a stated configuration fact, not an image-derived cause."}, {"observation": "Trunk surface is entirely smooth: no retained leaf-base stubs, no spiral diamond lattice, no fibrous matting.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner states the trunk organs (fn-110) have not landed; that accounts for the absence without resolving the core traits."}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit bunches or inflorescence stalks at the crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner states the date cluster (fn-111) has not landed. Note also that only reference-0 evidences fruit and only at one maturity state; sex and season would affect a live specimen, but the inventory records this trait as core."}, {"observation": "A single unbranched stem carries the whole crown, with no branches and no foliage on the trunk at either seed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the render trunk, satisfying the owner's third priority at both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The P-BASE render is a flat black silhouette filling most of the frame with no resolvable surface detail.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with a camera placed inside or hard against the trunk, or with the recorded hidden visibility for this input; not determinable from the image alone."}, {"observation": "Foliage colour and overall trunk lean fall within the inventory's recorded reference spread.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Dead-frond skirt, orange petiole sheathing, basal leaflet spines and trunk weathering colour are absent from the render.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Render crown is a flat radial fan of short straight axes with no arch and no fronds descending below the crown base; reference crown is a rounded shuttlecock of long outward-then-downward arching fronds. Defining mismatch at both seeds."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Leaflets appear as sparse speckles and short stubs on largely bare rachides, with no plumose V-section and no continuous bristly margin as in all three references."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The drawn trunk is a smooth untextured tube over its full visible length; the references show a coarse spiral diamond lattice of projecting stubs. Assessed as drawn, not invented; the owner's note that fn-110 has not landed explains but does not resolve it."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No fibre or shredded husk anywhere on the render trunk, against the packed reddish-brown matting filling the lattice in reference-1/reference-2."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Single unbranched stem is supported, but the columnar near-constant diameter is not: the render trunk tapers strongly from flared base to narrow apex and bulges at the mid-trunk knee, where reference-1/reference-2 hold near-constant diameter."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "No stalks or fruit bunches drawn at the crown; reference-0 shows two to three heavy pendent orange-red bunches. Owner-scoped out (fn-111) but not resolved."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary. No collar of dead brown fronds beneath the living crown in either render; reference-0 shows a distinct skirt against the upper trunk. Non-blocking refinement."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait, inventory-flagged uncertain. Render green sits inside the recorded deep-green to grey-glaucous reference spread; treated as acceptable variation."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. The crown apex in both P-WHOLE renders is a small dark cluster a few pixels across; petiole base colour is not resolvable at this scale."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait covering lean and single curve only. The render's overall lean is within the reference range; its high-frequency waviness and angular knee are charged against owner-trunk-straight-constant and solitary-columnar-stem, not here."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait the inventory records as scene-dependent. The bare render trunk matches reference-0 and satisfies the owner's requirement that nothing grow on the trunk."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary. Render trunk is a uniform dark grey-brown with a smooth specular gradient and no weathering variation, lighter stub faces or bleaching. Non-blocking refinement."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary, inventory-flagged uncertain. Both P-WHOLE renders widen into a broad base meeting the ground, consistent at silhouette level with reference-0; no finer claim is made."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. No smooth green crownshaft is present in the renders; frond bases sit directly on the trunk, as in reference-1."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary, inventory-flagged uncertain in the references themselves. The render's proximal frond region is unresolved speckle, so presence or absence cannot be read."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Variation trait, but the render sits outside the recorded range rather than within it: crown spread is a small multiple of trunk width and frond length is roughly a sixth of trunk height, far short of reference-0 where frond length is a substantial fraction of the visible trunk."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"13b5d2f2-b6e7-4f22-8f36-4950c1573ea8","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump"